Section 7.6 detection detecting goal
misgeneralization is harder than

2
00:00:05,919 --> 00:00:10,439
detecting misspecification during
training. The core difficulty is that

3
00:00:10,439 --> 00:00:14,439
goal misgeneralization often looks like
success until the distribution

4
00:00:14,439 --> 00:00:18,879
shifts enough to reveal the proxy.
Behavioral indistinguishability during

5
00:00:18,879 --> 00:00:21,879
training means that there's no obvious
failure signal to

6
00:00:21,879 --> 00:00:25,960
detect. This makes it fundamentally
different from capability failures

7
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:28,989
or or specification problems, where we can
often spot

8
00:00:28,989 --> 00:00:33,310
issues through poor performance or obvious
misinterpretation of instructions.

9
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:38,390
Goal misgeneralization spans a continuous
spectrum from simple proxy

10
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:42,869
correlations to sophisticated scheming
behavior. At one end we

11
00:00:42,869 --> 00:00:46,909
have straightforward cases where models
learn simple correlated heuristics.

12
00:00:47,390 --> 00:00:50,549
At the other end we have adversarial goal
directed

13
00:00:50,549 --> 00:00:54,590
systems that strategically conceal their
true objectives while appearing

14
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:58,920
aligned. Each point on this spectrum
requires different detection

15
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:01,799
approaches, but they all share the same
basic common

16
00:01:01,799 --> 00:01:04,680
thread, the gap between what we intended
the system

17
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:08,000
to learn and what it actually learned. No
single

18
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,519
detection method will catch all forms of
goal misgeneralization.

19
00:01:12,159 --> 00:01:15,239
Simple proxy learning might be caught
through careful test

20
00:01:15,239 --> 00:01:20,400
set design and distribution shift
analysis. Sophisticated deception requires

21
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:25,019
monitoring internal reasoning processes or
setting up adversarial evaluation

22
00:01:25,099 --> 00:01:28,540
scenarios. This means we need what we've
been emphasizing

23
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:32,459
throughout this book, defense in depth. We
can apply

24
00:01:32,459 --> 00:01:36,980
this principle recursively even within the
specific subproblem of

25
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:41,819
detecting goal misgeneralization. We need
multiple complementary approaches that

26
00:01:41,819 --> 00:01:46,500
provide uncorrelated signals about system
behavior. We organize detection

27
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:50,379
approaches using the same taxonomy from
our evaluations chapter

28
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:55,180
by how they gather evidence about AI
systems Behavioral

29
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:58,340
monitoring examines what models do through
their inputs and

30
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:04,140
outputs. Internal state monitoring uses
interpretability techniques to examine

31
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:08,580
how models think. Environmental monitoring
watches for the downstream

32
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:12,539
effects of misaligned behavior. For each
approach, we face

33
00:02:12,539 --> 00:02:15,699
the same temporal trade off. Earlier
detection is less

34
00:02:15,699 --> 00:02:19,349
reliable but more actionable, while later
detection is more

35
00:02:19,349 --> 00:02:24,430
reliable but potentially too late for
intervention. Behavioral techniques

