fakers represent a

247
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:26,899
latent variable that tracks p safe to
behave and

248
00:16:26,899 --> 00:16:30,899
two alignment fakers reveal misalignment
when the variable exceeds

249
00:16:30,899 --> 00:16:34,740
a threshold. To pinpoint this latent
variable, we use

250
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:38,299
scenarios where p safety to misbehave
varies and where

251
00:16:38,299 --> 00:16:41,009
models are still benign. The green region
in the

252
00:16:41,009 --> 00:16:45,929
figure the effectiveness of activation
manipulation reveals fundamental
differences

253
00:16:45,929 --> 00:16:50,009
in how aligned and misaligned goals are
computationally represented.

254
00:16:50,649 --> 00:16:53,850
Models that learn to misbehave faster when
fine tuned

255
00:16:53,850 --> 00:16:58,210
toward misaligned behaviors compared to
genuinely aligned models suggest

256
00:16:58,210 --> 00:17:02,610
that misaligned objectives may involve
simpler computational pathways that

257
00:17:02,610 --> 00:17:05,690
are easier to activate when normal
processing is disrupted.

258
00:17:06,190 --> 00:17:09,950
The success of noise injection indicates
that strategic concealment

259
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:14,269
requires additional computational overhead
that becomes harder to maintain

260
00:17:14,589 --> 00:17:18,789
when the model's regulatory mechanisms are
impaired. Similar to

261
00:17:18,789 --> 00:17:24,269
how disinhibiting substances affect human
behavior, activation manipulation
techniques

262
00:17:24,269 --> 00:17:28,950
demonstrate computational vulnerabilities
in goal misgeneralization that can be

263
00:17:28,950 --> 00:17:32,990
exploited for detection purposes. The
differential response to noise

264
00:17:32,990 --> 00:17:36,950
injection suggests that misaligned goals
exist as relatively fragile

265
00:17:36,950 --> 00:17:40,410
computational patterns, patterns that
become more apparent when disrupted.

266
00:17:40,970 --> 00:17:44,170
However, the technique achieved limited
success with only mild

267
00:17:44,170 --> 00:17:48,369
effects in some settings. Fuzzing
increased information revelation rates

268
00:17:48,369 --> 00:17:51,650
to below 1% in certain experiments,
suggesting it may

269
00:17:51,650 --> 00:17:54,890
be more effective when combined with other
detection approaches

270
00:17:54,890 --> 00:18:00,849
rather than used in isolation. Reasoning
Structure analysis Analysis

271
00:18:00,849 --> 00:18:04,380
of reasoning step importance can reveal
when models are

272
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:10,259
pursuing misaligned goals by identifying
thought anchors. Critical reasoning

273
00:18:10,259 --> 00:18:16,140
steps that disproportionately influence
subsequent reasoning techniques like
counterfactual

274
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:21,539
resampling, generating alternative
continuations from each reasoning step,
and

275
00:18:21,539 --> 00:18:24,900
attention analysis can identify which
parts of a reasoning

276
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:28,180
trace are most causally important for the
final answer.

277
00:18:28,579 --> 00:18:32,440
Planning and backtracking steps can
consistently show higher importance

278
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:37,160
than computational steps, suggesting that
goal directed reasoning operates

279
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:40,680
through high level organizational
sentences that steer the overall

280
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:44,559
trajectory. This could help detect cases
where models are

281
00:18:44,559 --> 00:18:48,559
reasoning toward misaligned objectives by
revealing when planning steps

282
00:18:48,559 --> 00:18:53,759
point toward problematic goals. Combined
techniques the defense in

283
00:18:53,759 --> 00:18:58,500
depth detection techniques would combine
multiple interpretability techniques with

284
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:03,019
behavioral monitoring to create
uncorrelated detection signals. As an

285
00:19:03,019 --> 00:19:06,980
illustrative example, a comprehensive
System might use SAEs to

286
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:11,619
identify suspicious features in model
activations, validate their importance

287
00:19:11,619 --> 00:19:16,299
through activation patching experiments,
test their generalization through probe

288
00:19:16,299 --> 00:19:20,660
analysis, and correlate findings with
behavioral anomalies detected through

289
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:25,660
